question_text:
Given the following function under the default coercive mode, what is the behavior when a float is passed to the integer parameter?

```php
function setAge(int $age) {
    return $age;
}
setAge(25.8);
```

Given the following code:

```php
declare(strict_types=1);
function add(int $a, int $b): int {
    return $a + $b;
}
```

How does the `declare(strict_types=1);` directive affect function argument and return type validation in this script? (PHP 7.0+)

What arguments can be passed to the parameter in the following function declaration? (PHP 7.1+)

```php
function process(iterable $items) {
    foreach ($items as $item) {
        // ...
    }
}
```

Which return type declaration in the following function enforces that the function cannot return any value, not even null? (PHP 7.1+)

```php
function logMessage(string $msg): void {
    echo $msg;
}
```

What is the behavior of the `never` return type in the following function declaration? (PHP 8.1+)

```php
function redirect(string $url): never {
    header("Location: $url");
    exit;
}
```

Given the following code declarations, what is the difference between Union Types (used in `accept`) and Intersection Types (used in `process`)? (PHP 8.1+)

```php
function accept(HTMLRequest|APIRequest $request) {}
function process(Logger&Serializable $object) {}
```

Is the following function declaration with a standalone `null` return type valid in PHP? (PHP 8.2+)

```php
function getNothing(): null {
    return null;
}
```

Under what condition will accessing the uninitialized variable in a context like this cause a Fatal Error (Error exception) instead of a Warning/Notice? (PHP 8.0+)

```php
class Profile {
    public string $bio;
}
$profile = new Profile();
echo $profile->bio;
```

Given the following function definition, what is the return type behavior when a function is declared to return `false`? (PHP 8.2+)

```php
function getStatus(): false {
    return false;
}
```

What is the output of the following code snippet?

```php
$x = 'y';
$y = 'z';
echo $$x;
```

Given the following code snippet, what is the behavior and lifetime of the static variable `$count`?

```php
function counter() {
    static $count = 0;
    $count++;
    return $count;
}
```

Given the following code, how can the function `printGlobal()` access the variable `$globalVar` without using the `global` keyword?

```php
$globalVar = "Hello World";
function printGlobal() {
    // Access $globalVar here
}
```

Given the two blocks of code below, how do their comparison behaviors differ? (PHP 8.0+)

```php
// Block A (switch)
switch ($value) {
    case '1': echo 'string'; break;
}

// Block B (match)
match ($value) {
    '1' => 'string',
};
```

What is a dangerous side effect of using the reference in the first loop in this code?

```php
$array = [1, 2, 3];
foreach ($array as &$value) {
    // do nothing
}
// $value is not unset
```

Given the following statements, what is the difference in error behavior if the file `missing.php` does not exist?

```php
// Statement A
include 'missing.php';

// Statement B
require 'missing.php';
```

Based on the restrictions of the `goto` statement in PHP, why is a jump like the one in Block B invalid?

```php
// Block A (Valid)
goto end;
end:

// Block B (Invalid)
goto loop_body;
for ($i = 0; $i < 10; $i++) {
    loop_body:
}
```

Given the two ways of defining constants below, how do they differ under the hood?

```php
// Method A
const MAX_LIMIT = 100;

// Method B
define('MIN_LIMIT', 10);
```

What is the output of the following code snippet without break statements?

```php
$value = 1;
switch ($value) {
    case 1:
        echo "One ";
    case 2:
        echo "Two ";
    default:
        echo "Default";
}
```

What happens when the following match expression is executed? (PHP 8.0+)

```php
$value = 3;
$result = match ($value) {
    1 => 'One',
    2 => 'Two',
};
```

What is the behavior when accessing `$result` after the loop exits in the code below?

```php
for ($i = 0; $i < 3; $i++) {
    $result = $i * 2;
}
echo $result;
```

Given the following code, what is the scope of the variable `$innerVar` defined inside the nested function?

```php
function outer() {
    function inner() {
        $innerVar = "nested";
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following code?

```php
$a = 1;
function test() {
    echo $a;
}
test();
```

Given the following class definition, what is the default visibility of `getName()`?

```php
class User {
    function getName() {
        return "John";
    }
}
```

Given the following code skeleton, which keyword must replace the placeholder, and how many parent classes can the child class inherit from?

```php
class Animal {}
class Dog ??? Animal {}
```

Consider the following definitions:

```php
abstract class BaseController {
    public string $theme = 'default';
    public function render() { /* concrete implementation */ }
}

interface Loggable {
    public function log(string $message);
}
```

Based on this, what is a key difference between abstract classes and interfaces?

Given the following usage of a Trait, what is its primary purpose?

```php
trait Shareable {
    public function share($item) { /* code */ }
}

class Post {
    use Shareable;
}
```

What is the behavior of the anonymous class in the following instantiation? (PHP 7.0+)

```php
$logger = new class {
    public function log($msg) {
        echo $msg;
    }
};
```

Given the following class definition with a readonly property, which of the rules applies? (PHP 8.1+)

```php
class User {
    public readonly string $username;
    public function __construct(string $username) {
        $this->username = $username;
    }
}
```

What is the effect of declaring the class as readonly in the following example? (PHP 8.2+)

```php
readonly class Post {
    public string $title;
    public string $content;
}
```

Given the following declaration in PHP 8.4, how does the asymmetric visibility of the property behave?

```php
class Book {
    public private(set) string $title;
}
```

Given the following parent class, what is the consequence of marking the method as final?

```php
class Base {
    final public function execute() {
        // ...
    }
}
```

What will the call to `ChildClass::test()` print, illustrating late static binding? (PHP 5.3+)

```php
class ParentClass {
    public static function getClassName() { return 'ParentClass'; }
    public static function test() {
        echo self::getClassName() . ' ' . static::getClassName();
    }
}
class ChildClass extends ParentClass {
    public static function getClassName() { return 'ChildClass'; }
}
```

Is the following override of an interface constant valid in a class? (PHP 8.3+)

```php
interface MyInterface {
    const VERSION = '1.0';
}
class MyClass implements MyInterface {
    public const VERSION = '2.0';
}
```

Given the following code, which operator/keyword must replace the placeholder to resolve the conflict between the two traits?

```php
trait A { public function talk() { echo 'A'; } }
trait B { public function talk() { echo 'B'; } }
class Talker {
    use A, B {
        A::talk ??? B;
    }
}
```

Given the following class definition, what is the default visibility of `$value`?

```php
class Container {
    var $value = 10;
}
```

What is the behavior of the following class when implementing two interfaces that declare the same method?

```php
interface Reader { public function read(): string; }
interface Scanner { public function read(): string; }
class Device implements Reader, Scanner {
    public function read(): string {
        return "data";
    }
}
```

Given the following code snippet, which operator and keywords are used to access the static property `$count`?

```php
class Tracker {
    public static int $count = 0;
    public static function increment() {
        self::$count++;
    }
}
```

What is the result of executing the following instantiation?

```php
abstract class Shape {
    abstract public function getArea(): float;
}
$shape = new Shape();
```

Given the two definitions below, what difference in method visibility rules applies?

```php
interface Logger {
    public function log(string $msg);
}

abstract class BaseLogger {
    abstract protected function write(string $msg);
}
```

Given the following code snippet using PHP 8.4 features, what feature is being demonstrated and what is its purpose?

```php
class User {
    public string $name {
        set => trim($value);
        get => ucfirst($this->name);
    }
}
```

Given the following code snippet, if trait `$count` is incremented in class `A`, what is true about static properties in traits?

```php
trait Counter {
    public static int $count = 0;
}
class A { use Counter; }
class B { use Counter; }
```

Is the declaration syntax in the following code block valid in PHP?

```php
interface Runnable {}
interface Loggable {}
class Task {}

class Worker extends Task implements Runnable, Loggable {}
```

What properties and assignment operations are implicitly generated by the following constructor property promotion? (PHP 8.0+)

```php
class User {
    public function __construct(
        public string $name,
        protected int $age
    ) {}
}
```

Given the class below, under what condition will the `__destruct` magic method be called?

```php
class Session {
    public function __destruct() {
        // clean up resource
    }
}
```

In the following class, under what condition are the `__get` and `__set` magic methods triggered?

```php
class Registry {
    private array $data = [];
    public function __get($name) { return $this->data[$name] ?? null; }
    public function __set($name, $value) { $this->data[$name] = $value; }
}
```

Given the class below, which calls on `$user` will trigger the `__isset` magic method?

```php
class User {
    private array $properties = ['email' => 'test@example.com'];
    public function __isset($name) {
        return isset($this->properties[$name]);
    }
}
$user = new User();
```

Given the following class declaration, when are `__call` and `__callStatic` triggered?

```php
class Proxy {
    public function __call($name, $arguments) {}
    public static function __callStatic($name, $arguments) {}
}
```

What requirement must the `__toString` magic method satisfy in the class below to avoid a TypeError?

```php
class Document {
    public function __toString() {
        return 'document content';
    }
}
```

Given the class below, what does the implementation of the `__invoke` magic method allow you to do with an instance of `Calculator`?

```php
class Calculator {
    public function __invoke($a, $b) {
        return $a + $b;
    }
}
```

Given the code below, how is the `__clone` magic method utilized?

```php
class Profile {
    public string $name;
    public function __clone() {
        // custom clone logic
    }
}
$p1 = new Profile();
$p2 = clone $p1;
```

What are the roles of the `__serialize` and `__unserialize` magic methods in the class below? (PHP 7.4+)

```php
class Settings {
    private array $data;
    public function __serialize(): array { return $this->data; }
    public function __unserialize(array $data): void { $this->data = $data; }
}
```

Given the following class declaration, which method will PHP execute when calling `serialize()` on an instance? (PHP 7.4+)

```php
class Migration {
    public function __sleep() { return ['legacy']; }
    public function __serialize() { return ['modern']; }
}
```

Under what condition is the static `__set_state` magic method called in the class below?

```php
class Config {
    public static function __set_state($array) {
        // ...
    }
}
```

What is the purpose of the `__debugInfo` magic method in the following class?

```php
class Secrets {
    private string $password = 'secret';
    public function __debugInfo() {
        return ['password' => '***'];
    }
}
```

Which parameters must the `__call` magic method accept?

```php
class Dynamic {
    public function __call(string $name, array $arguments) {
        // ...
    }
}
```

What happens if you try to execute the code below when `__unset` is not defined?

```php
class User {
    protected string $email = 'test@example.com';
}
$user = new User();
unset($user->email);
```

Is the following declaration of `__get` valid and free from warnings in modern PHP?

```php
class Config {
    private function __get($name) {
        // ...
    }
}
```

Given the following code skeleton, how do standard Closures in PHP import variables from the parent (outer) scope?

```php
$message = "hello";
$greet = function() use ($message) {
    echo $message;
};
```

What is the output of the code below, demonstrating the variable capturing behavior of Arrow Functions? (PHP 7.4+)

```php
$factor = 10;
$multiplier = fn($num) => $num * $factor;
$factor = 20;
echo $multiplier(2);
```

Given the signatures of these two array functions, what is the argument order difference?

```php
array_map(callable $callback, array $array, ...$arrays);
array_filter(array $array, callable $callback);
```

What is the output/return value of the following array_reduce call?

```php
$result = array_reduce([], function($carry, $item) {
    return $carry + $item;
});
var_dump($result);
```

Given the following array find call, what does it return? (PHP 8.4+)

```php
$array = [10, 20, 30, 40];
$result = array_find($array, fn($val) => $val > 25);
```

What does the following array_any expression evaluate to? (PHP 8.4+)

```php
$array = [2, 4, 6, 7];
$result = array_any($array, fn($val) => $val % 2 !== 0);
```

What does the following array_all expression evaluate to? (PHP 8.4+)

```php
$array = [2, 4, 6, 8];
$result = array_all($array, fn($val) => $val % 2 === 0);
```

Which of the following fn statements is a valid arrow function syntax in PHP? (PHP 7.4+)

```php
// Option A
$fn = fn($x) => $x * 2;

// Option B
$fn = fn($x) => {
    $val = $x * 2;
    return $val;
};
```

Which catch block syntax is correct for catching multiple exceptions in a single block? (PHP 7.1+)

```php
try {
    processData();
} catch (??? $e) {
    logError($e);
}
```

When is the `finally` block executed in the following structure?

```php
try {
    doSomething();
    return true;
} catch (Exception $e) {
    logError($e);
} finally {
    cleanup();
}
```

Which of the following usages is allowed because `throw` is an expression in PHP 8.0+?

```php
// Usage A
$name = $input ?? throw new InvalidArgumentException("Name required");

// Usage B
$fn = fn() => throw new Exception("Error");
```

What happens to the first exception if a second exception is thrown inside the `finally` block in this code?

```php
try {
    throw new Exception("First");
} finally {
    throw new Exception("Second");
}
```

Under what condition is an ArgumentCountError thrown in the following code context? (PHP 7.0+)

```php
function greet(string $name, string $greeting) {
    return "$greeting, $name";
}
greet("Alice");
```

Can you throw an instance of a class that does not implement the Throwable interface, as shown in this code? (PHP 7.0+)

```php
class CustomObject {}
throw new CustomObject();
```
